# Kode.Mini Governance

## Purpose

This document describes how Kode.Mini projects are maintained.

## Maintainers

Maintainers are responsible for:

* Reviewing contributions.
* Maintaining project quality.
* Managing releases.
* Addressing Issues.
* Responding to security reports.
* Protecting project infrastructure.

## Contributors

Contributors may:

* Report bugs.
* Request features.
* Submit Pull Requests.
* Improve documentation.
* Help test projects.

Contributors do not automatically receive administrative access.

## Repository permissions

Access should follow the principle of least privilege.

Typical roles are:

* Owner — organization administration
* Maintainer — project maintenance
* Developer — code contributions
* Triage — Issues and Pull Requests
* Read — viewing the project

## Decisions

Technical decisions should normally be discussed through Issues, Pull Requests, or project discussions.

Security-sensitive decisions may be handled privately.

## Changes to governance

The maintainers may update this document as Kode.Mini grows.
